> 2^10
1024
> it(x: i8) = x^2
> range it
range of it -> i8:
  -127..121   (44 distinct values)
  values: -127, -124, -119, -112..-111, -103, -95, -92, -87, -79, -71, -63, -60, -55, -47, -39, -31, -28, -23, -15, -7, 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, ...
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> it(x) = sin(x^2)
> diff it x
d/dx it = 2x*cos(x^2)
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 3e-10)
> it(x) = x^3 - 3*x
> crit it
critical points of it:
  it' = 3x^2 - 3
  x ≈ -1: local maximum, it = 2
  x ≈ 1: local minimum, it = -2
  searched [-10, 10] (default; give x a range)
> it(x: i8) = x*2 + 1
> wrap it
wrap analysis of it:
  2x   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  2x + 1   (i8)
      nuw holds
      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      exact for: -64..63
  over all 256 points of the domain
> it(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b)/2
> that(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b)/2
> equiv it that
it and that are equal on the domain of it (exhaustive)
> it(x) = x^2*sin(x)
> integrate it from 0 to pi
∫ x^2*sin(x) dx
  = 2x*sin(x) + 2cos(x) - x^2*cos(x) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 3.14159] (max difference 8.9e-16)
  from 0 to 3.14159: F(3.14159) - F(0) = 5.86960440108936
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 5.86960440108936, estimated error 6.5e-14
  the two agree to 0
> it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)
> closed it
sum(i, 1, n, i^2)
  = n*(n + 1)*(2n + 1)/6
  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)
  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain
> it(x) = sin(2*x)
> periodic it
periodic it:
  yes: fundamental period pi ≈ 3.141592654
  proved symbolically: sin(2x) has period pi; x occurs only inside them, so f(x + p) = f(x).  Smallest: no p/k (2 <= k <= 64) is a period (checked at 997 points)
> identify y'' + y = 0
identify y'' + y = 0:
  an ordinary differential equation of order 2 in y(t)
  linear: every y-term appears to the first power [proved: the partial derivatives in y, y', ... do not involve y]
  homogeneous
  constant coefficients (and autonomous)
  characteristic equation: r^2 + 1 = 0, roots ±i
  homogeneous solutions: y(t) = a combination of cos(t), sin(t)
  autonomous: the independent variable does not appear explicitly
  solved for the highest derivative: y'' = -y  (then initial values and: dsolve y)
> sqrt(16)
4
> it(x) = sin(x)/x
> limit it x -> 0
limit of it as x -> 0:
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x))/(1) = lim cos(x)
  = 1 (from both sides)
  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1
    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1
    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees
